<score-partwise>
  <work>
    <work-title>Now Sin, With Reign Unbroken</work-title>
  </work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">Words: Thomas Hansen Kingo, 1699. Translated by Paul Christian Paulsen, 1927.
Music: 'Au Meines Herzens Grunde' or 'I Døden Jesus Blunded' or 'Jeg Vil Din Pris Udsjunge', David Wolder, 1598.
Setting: "Hymnal for Church and Home" (Danish Evangelical Lutheran Synods), 1927.
copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2025 Revision.</creator>
    <encoding>
      <encoder>abc2xml version 268</encoder>
      <software>https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/abc2xml.html</software>
      <encoding-date>2026-09-07</encoding-date>
    </encoding>
    <source>Music and Lyrics source: "Hymnal for Church and Home", Danish Evangelical Lutheran Synods, 1927 Hymn 157.
Tune first published in David Wolder's Neu Catechismus Gesangbüchlein, Hamburg, 1598
Note that this arrangement actually tweaks the original melody here and there, but without changing the meter.  Thus the soprano line does not fully match the same tune for different texts in different hymnals.  I assume that both those changes and the arrangement are probably the work of the hymnal team of 1927.</source>
  </identification>
